{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["(And why do You dwell among them and cherish them?) — For there is no divination in Jacob, etc. — They do not practice soothsaying and sorcery as we do, nor do they inquire of a medium and a spirit-knowers, but rather — 'At this time it will be said to Jacob and to Israel what El has wrought' — because the Shekhinah is among them, the prophets say to Jacob and to Israel today what the Holy One, blessed be He, has wrought and decreed for the days to come, and they have no need for divination and sorcery." "'At this time it will be said' — that which is destined to come at a time within many days and years, He will declare to them through a prophet. And so every instance of 'כעת' speaking of future things. As is written regarding Manoah's wife: ״לוּ חָפֵץ יְהוָה לְהָמִיתֵנוּ״ — now — ״לֹא לָקַח מִיָּדֵנוּ עֹלָה וּמִנְחָה״, and ״כָּעֵת לֹא הִשְׁמִיעָנוּ כָּזֹאת״ — the birth of the son, about which He informed us that it would be ״כָּעֵת״ in the coming year — He did not make us hear; rather, we shall surely live and a son will be fulfilled for us, for if we were to die, how would we have a son next year? And similarly: ״כָּעֵת חַיָּה אֶת חוֹבֶקֶת בֵּן״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:59.323341958Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}